  "footnotes": [
    "Frank Coyle, 30+ years teaching CS, currently at UC Berkeley. ~21-minute conference talk to a ~5,000-person developer audience.",
    "Opens and closes with Sister Corita Kent / John Cage: \"Nothing is a mistake. There is no win. There's no fail. There's only make.\"",
    "Historical thread: neuro-symbolic AI is not a new invention — it's the return of 1980s expert systems, dressed for LLM-era problems (~14:16). The AI winter's ghost frames the whole talk as recursive history.",
    "Load-bearing prescription (~18:25): \"Pydantic at the door, ontology at the ledger, and pure agents — your agents should try to have no side effects.\"",
    "For the ZP corpus: partial resonance. Coyle's \"run them through the ontology first\" is a per-domain semantic-validation gate — architecturally analogous to a chain-anchored audit substrate that refuses ill-formed delegation acts. Different content, same structural role."
  ]
